igh-level-sdk#consumer-builder-options","content":"Commit after each message is received"},"2437":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/high-level-sdk-146","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/high-level-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/high-level-sdk#consumer-builder-options","content":"Disabled"},"2438":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/high-level-sdk-147","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/high-level-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/high-level-sdk#consumer-builder-options","content":"Commit manually"},"2439":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/high-level-sdk-148","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/high-level-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/high-level-sdk#manual-offset-control","content":"With AutoCommitMode.Disabled, commit offsets yourself via the consumer's StoreOffsetAsync:"},"2440":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/high-level-sdk-149","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/high-level-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/high-level-sdk#manual-offset-control","content":"StoreOffsetAsync(offset, partitionId, resetLastPolled = false) stores the offset for a partition; pass resetLastPolled: true to also move the consumer's cached last-polled position so the next poll resumes past the stored offset. DeleteOffsetAsync(partitionId) clears the stored offset."},"2441":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/high-level-sdk-150","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/high-level-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/high-level-sdk#consumer-groups","content":"Pass a Consumer.Group(...) and let the builder create and join the group for load-balanced consumption:"},"2442":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/high-level-sdk-151","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/high-level-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/high-level-sdk#consuming-with-rented-buffers","content":"ReceiveAsync copies each payload into its own byte[]. ReceiveRentedAsync is the high-level counterpart of the low-level rented poll API: payloads are slices of a pooled buffer shared by all messages from the same poll. Each yielded ReceivedRentedMessage must be disposed — the buffer returns to the pool once the last message of its batch is disposed:"},"2443":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/high-level-sdk-152","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/high-level-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/high-level-sdk#consuming-with-rented-buffers","content":"ReceivedRentedMessage (IDisposable) exposes Message (a RentedMessageResponse), CurrentOffset, PartitionId, Status, and Error. This path performs no deserialization, so Status is always Success. Payload and raw-header memory are only valid until the message is disposed — copy out anything you need to keep (e.g. message.Message.Payload.ToArray())."},"2444":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/high-level-sdk-153","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/high-level-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/high-level-sdk#consuming-with-rented-buffers","content":"Auto-commit modes apply exactly as with ReceiveAsync. Forgetting to dispose a message never corrupts data — the batch buffer simply isn't returned to the pool and is reclaimed by the GC as an ordinary allocation."},"2445":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/high-level-sdk-154","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/high-level-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/high-level-sdk#typed-consumer","content":"For automatic deserialization, use IggyConsumerBuilder<T> with an IDeserializer<T> and iterate with ReceiveDeserializedAsync. Each ReceivedMessage<T> carries a Status you should check:"},"2446":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/high-level-sdk-155","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/high-level-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/high-level-sdk#typed-consumer","content":"Note: On the typed builders, the fluent With* methods are inherited from the untyped base builder and return the base type, while the typed Build() hides the base one. Chaining Create(...).WithAutoCommitMode(...).Build() therefore resolves to the base Build() and returns an untyped consumer/publisher. Keep the typed builder in a variable (as above) and call Build() on it — the With* calls mutate the builder, so their return value can be ignored."},"2447":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro","type":"page","content":"C# SDK","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","SDK","C#"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro"},"2448":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro-0","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro#installation","content":"Installation"},"2449":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro-1","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro#supported-protocols","content":"Supported protocols"},"2450":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro-2","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro#creating-a-client","content":"Creating a client"},"2451":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro-3","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro#quick-start","content":"Quick start"},"2452":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro-4","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro#producer","content":"Producer"},"2453":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro-5","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro#consumer","content":"Consumer"},"2454":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro-6","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro#next-steps","content":"Next steps"},"2455":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro-7","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro","content":"The Iggy SDK for C# is a modern, async-first client library for interacting with an Iggy message streaming server from your .NET applications. It supports TCP and HTTP transports. The package is available on NuGet and the source code lives on GitHub."},"2456":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro-8","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro","content":"The SDK is built around the IIggyClient interface, which aggregates every feature (publishing, consuming, stream/topic management, users, offsets, consumer groups, and system operations). For the low-level per-call API and the full configuration reference, see the Guide. For the ergonomic, batteries-included producer/consumer abstractions, see the High-level SDK."},"2457":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro-9","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro#supported-protocols","content":"The SDK supports two transport protocols:"},"2458":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro-10","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro#supported-protocols","content":"TCP — binary protocol for optimal performance and lower latency (recommended)"},"2459":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro-11","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro#supported-protocols","content":"HTTP — RESTful JSON API for stateless operations"},"2460":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro-12","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro#supported-protocols","content":"Some operations are TCP-only and throw FeatureUnavailableException on HTTP: joining/leaving a consumer group, GetMeAsync, and DeleteSegmentsAsync."},"2461":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro-13","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro#creating-a-client","content":"Create a client with IggyClientFactory.CreateClient, then call ConnectAsync:"},"2462":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro-14","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro#creating-a-client","content":"Optionally, provide an ILoggerFactory for diagnostics (defaults to NullLoggerFactory.Instance):"},"2463":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro-15","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro#creating-a-client","content":"IggyClientConfigurator also exposes buffer sizes, TLS, automatic reconnection with exponential backoff, auto-login (so you can skip the explicit LoginUserAsync call), and client-side message encryption. See Client configuration for the full reference."},"2464":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro-16","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro#quick-start","content":"These samples use the High-level SDK — the recommended way to build producers and consumers. For the equivalent low-level, per-call flow, see the Guide."},"2465":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro-17","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro#consumer","content":"ReceiveAsync polls indefinitely — pass a CancellationToken or break out of the loop to stop."},"2466":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro-18","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro#next-steps","content":"Guide — client configuration reference and the full API surface: auth, streams, topics, partitions, publishing, consuming, offsets, consumer groups, system operations"},"2467":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro-19","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro#next-steps","content":"High-level SDK — IggyPublisher / IggyConsumer with background sending, retries, auto-commit, typed (de)serialization, and pooled (rented) buffers for allocation-free hot paths"},"2468":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro-20","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/intro#next-steps","content":"Examples — producer, consumer-group, and typed-message samples, plus links to runnable projects"},"2469":{"id":"/docs/sdk/python/examples","page_id":"/docs/sdk/python/examples","type":"page","content":"Examples","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","SDK","Python"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdk/python/examples"},"2470":{"id":"/docs/sdk/python/examples-0","page_id":"/do