three replicas for one-node fault tolerance. A two-node cluster is useful for development, but it cannot make progress after either node fails."],[1995,"A complete getting-started example is available in the examples/go directory. It demonstrates connecting to the server, creating streams and topics, sending messages, and consuming them."],[2070,"A consumer that creates and joins a consumer group, commits offsets after each received message, and surfaces polling errors:"],[2247,"A convenience overload accepts a MessageFetchRequest if you prefer named fields:"],[759,"A flush is triggered when either the message count threshold (default 1024) or size threshold (default 1 MiB) is reached"],[2239,"A Message takes an id (Guid or UInt128) and a payload:"],[2250,"A MessageFetchRequest overload (PollMessagesRentedAsync(request)) is also available."],[2397,"A null message id sends the message with id 0, letting the server assign one."],[977,"A numeric value (e.g. 4) - exactly N shards"],[683,"A numeric value (e.g. 4) - exactly N shards pinned to cores 0..N"],[2069,"A publisher that creates the stream and topic if missing, batches sends in the background, and retries failures:"],[978,"A range (e.g. \"5..8\") - shards on cores 5, 6, 7"],[684,"A range (e.g. \"5..8\") - shards on specified core range"],[706,"A SegmentedLog with sealed segments and one active segment"],[2240,"A single-message overload is also available: SendMessagesAsync(streamId, topicId, partitioning, message)."],[1611,"A sink connector that consumes messages from Iggy streams and indexes them to Elasticsearch."],[2072,"A typed publisher/consumer pair that (de)serializes a record as JSON. Note that the typed builders are configured via statements rather than one fluent chain — the With* methods return the untyped base builder, so Build() must be called on the typed builder variable (see Typed consumer):"],[541,"About"],[1570,"Acting user"],[2564,"Add consumers dynamically at runtime."],[2570,"Add consumers dyna